      "end": 2.36,
      "text": "Hello, how's your day going?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 11.05,
      "end": 17.46,
      "text": "Look for the flattest patch you can find, a little higher than the ground around it. If it rains, low spots turn into puddles."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 21.64,
      "end": 27.68,
      "text": "Check the branches above it first. Dead limbs can drop in wind, so if anything looks cracked or bare, move away."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 35.91,
      "end": 39.92,
      "text": "Then skip that spot. Shade is lovely, but not worth a branch through the roof."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 43.65,
      "end": 50.2,
      "text": "Close enough to enjoy it, but at least a few big steps away, and not downwind. Sparks and nylon don't get along."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 56.02,
      "end": 59.15,
      "text": "That's it. Door facing away from the wind too, if you can."
